                <Param name="text" val="Let's have a practice. We will complete one short block, with N=2.&#10;&#10;For this practice, the sequence of previously displayed letters will be displayed at the top of the screen. The letter furthest to the right will be the previous letter (N=1).&#10;&#10;These practice trials will not time out, and feedback will be provided to help you learn. During the experiment you will need to remember the sequence and trials will time out fairly rapidly.&#10;&#10;For the first N letters you do not need to make any response as there is no &quot;N-back&quot; to compare to. This means in this block, where N=2, you should not press any button until at least the third letter appears.&#10;&#10;On every subsequent letter, you must decide if it is the same as the letter &quot;N back&quot;, and if it is, press the RIGHT ARROW key. If it is not the same letter as the one &quot;N back&quot;, do not press any buttons, and wait for the next letter.&#10;&#10;Press space to move to the next screen..." valType="str" updates="constant" plugin="None"/>
